-- title:
--   W(k)/pW(k)≅ k for perfect k of characteristic p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ which is perfect, in the sense that the $p$-power map on $k$ is bijective (`PerfectRing k p`). Let $\mathbb{W}(k) =$ `WittVector p k` be the ring of $p$-typical Witt vectors over $k$, and let `pIdeal p (WittVector p k)` denote the ideal generated by the single element $p$, that is $\mathrm{span}\{(p : \mathbb{W}(k))\} = p\,\mathbb{W}(k)$. The assertion is that the type of ring isomorphisms $k \simeq \mathbb{W}(k)/p\,\mathbb{W}(k)$ is nonempty: there exists an isomorphism of rings between $k$ and the quotient of the Witt vectors by the ideal generated by $p$. The statement is given in the existential (`Nonempty`) form, so it produces no designated isomorphism; the isomorphism constructed in the proof is the inverse of the one induced by the zeroth Witt coordinate $\mathbb{W}(k) \to k$.
--
--   This is the standard identification of the residue ring of the Witt vectors of a perfect field of characteristic $p$ with the field itself, the ring $\mathbb{W}(k)$ being the complete discrete valuation ring with residue field $k$. Within the Čerednik–Drinfeld material it is used to transfer field-theoretic and algebraic-closedness properties from $k$ to the base ring $\mathbb{W}(k)/p\,\mathbb{W}(k)$ over which special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules and Cartier quadruples are considered, and it is invoked by fourteen later results of that development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WittVector_nonempty_ringEquiv_quotient_pIdeal_of_perfectRing.lean

